这就像在一个漏斗里。无处可逃。对任何落下的东西都无处可逃。正是在一个类似于这个竖井的地方——皇后区的19号竖井，确实有东西掉下来了，而且是个大东西。去年11月，感恩节前一天，一个16吨重的绞车从竖井顶部的固定点脱落。汤姆·弗拉纳根（Tom Flanagan）和迈克·博伊斯（Mike Boyce）是八名在450英尺深处的猫道上工作的沙工中的两人，

25
00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:59.000
about 50 feet from the bottom when the huge winch plummeted downward. We know all of a sudden notice that cable got slack real fast and we looked up and all we see was this big snake coming out. It's the cable that's coming. And we couldn't see the surface due to the fog. So the cable was beating us up real bad, knocking everybody all about. And that big, big winch come through
距离底部约50英尺，这时巨大的绞车轰然坠落。我们突然发现电缆极快地松弛下来，我们抬头看，只见这条大蛇冲了出来。那是飞驰而来的电缆。由于雾气，我们看不到地面。所以电缆把我们抽打得非常惨，把所有人都撞得东倒西歪。然后那个巨大无比的绞车冲了下来，

26
00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:31.000
and all hell broke loose. Everything was flying all over and had no warning at all. He had a...I seen flashes out of the corner, am I right? I sounded like an explosion. Did that broke loose? And I was at my foot caught in a cable, my fingers and a grate hanging upside down. I was going to drop in a water or pick a brick while fall because I was slipping and like it's all the other guys I thought of my two kids and turn my hand around and the grate and stuck it in again and just let my foot loosen the
顿时乱作一团。所有东西都在飞舞，完全没有任何预警。他有一个……我眼角余光看到了闪光，对吗？听起来像是一次爆炸。那个脱落了？我的脚缠在电缆里，手指和格栅挂着，头朝下。我本要掉进水里或者坠落砸死，因为我在打滑，就像其他所有人一样，我想到了我的两个孩子，把手转过来抓住格栅，再次插进去，然后把脚从电缆里抽出来，

27
00:13:31.000 --> 00:14:21.000
cable and itch my way up to a good cable and pull myself up on the deform. I managed to get up to a flat piece of deck and just hang on, it'll piece a post on a guardrail and just hope them prayed until the dust settled until everything stopped coming. We were all very lucky that made it out of there. I just wish Anthony could have been as lucky as the rest of us. Anthony Odo was the 20th sandhog to be killed during construction of the water tunnel. That averages out to almost one fatality a year.
一路挪到一根好的电缆上，把自己拉到平台上。我设法爬到一块平坦的甲板上，紧紧抓住，抓住护栏上的一个柱子，只能祈祷灰尘落定、所有东西停止下落。我们能活着逃出来真是太幸运了。我只是希望安东尼能像我们其他人一样幸运。安东尼·奥多（Anthony Odo）是在水隧道建设期间丧生的第20名沙工。平均下来几乎是一年一人。

28
00:14:21.000 --> 00:15:07.000
You come here today to pray for the heroic men and women who made such tremendous sacrifices that the people of the city of New York would have water, life-giving water, for all the days of their lives and for generations yet to come. At St. Barnabas Church in the North Bronx, on senior coincidine holds a special mass each year in memory of the Sandhogs killed working on the water project. And so now we'll list the names of those if you stand as a tribute to men who have suffered a sacrifice for the work of our tunnel. Charles Specky Amina, Joseph Barton, the operating engineer, Stuart Birdzall. The first guy got killed on the water tunnel construction.
你们今天来这里，是为了祈祷那些做出巨大牺牲的英雄般的男女们，好让纽约市的人民拥有水，拥有生命之水，世世代代永享甘露。在北布朗克斯的圣巴拿巴教堂（St. Barnabas Church），高级神父科因蒂恩（ConCidine）每年都会举行一次特别弥撒，以纪念在水利工程施工中牺牲的沙工。现在我们将宣读这些人的名字，请大家起立，向为我们隧道工程作出牺牲的人们致敬。查尔斯·斯佩基·阿米娜（Charles Specky Amina）、约瑟夫·巴顿（Joseph Barton，操作工程师）、斯图尔特·伯德佐尔（Stuart Birdzall）。第一个在水隧道施工中丧生的人。

29
00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:43.000
Got killed about 20 feet away from me on a walk there. To hear that man moan with the pain. It was something, I mean, you know, I'll never forget that as long as I live you'll be Jay Horton minor Thanks sir one accident. I'll never forget brother in battery tunnel happened on Easter Saturday They put a guy on a motor That tunnel really had a bad slope and the great wonder about four degrees They were shutting the inside the lock
在猫道上距离我大约20英尺的地方被砸死。听到那个男人的痛苦呻吟。那真是一场……我的意思是，你知道的，我这辈子都不会忘记那件事。你将成为杰·霍尔顿（Jay Horton），矿工。谢谢先生。一次事故。我永远不会忘记，在复活节星期六，电池隧道发生的事情。他们把一个人放在一辆机车上。那条隧道坡度真的很陡，大约有四度。他们在锁孔里面关门。

30
00:15:43.000 --> 00:16:19.000
He came down with the motor he couldn't stop at the breakman jump, broke his leg, he hit the door, the battery jumped up, caught him in half. They come in and they got Andy and Andy took me with him and went over and put him in a sack and brought him out. I vomited the whole night. Yeah And that's what I would like to do. That's it. Lord have mercy. Christ have mercy. Lord have mercy. For every sandhawk who is killed on the job, there are hundreds, maybe thousands, of close calls.
他连着机车冲了下来，刹车失灵，刹车手跳车摔断了腿，他撞上了门，机车弹起来，将他拦腰截断。他们进来后找到了安迪，安迪带上我和他一起过去，把他装进麻袋带了出去。我吐了一整夜。是的。这就是我想做的。就这样。主啊，怜悯我们。基督，怜悯我们。主啊，怜悯我们。每一个在工作中丧生的沙工背后，都有成百上千次、甚至上万次死里逃生的经历。

31
00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:40.000
The most legendary took place in 1916. As the story goes, Marshall maybe was working in compressed air in a tunnel below the East River. There was a blowout. Maybe in two other sand dogs were shot out through a hole and up through the riverbed on a geyser, 25 feet high. They were mining and they didn't have the equipment in there and up to stop that blow.
最传奇的一次发生在1916年。故事是这样的，马歇尔·梅比（Marshall Maybie）当时正在东河下方的一条隧道里进行压缩空气作业。发生了一次井喷。梅比和其他两名沙工被一股25英尺高的间歇泉从洞口冲出，直冲上河床。他们当时正在掘进，那里没有设备来阻止那场井喷。

32
00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:56.000
And he tried to stop it and he went up through the river with two other guys. And he survived. The other two went died. The story seemed to catch attention because Marshall maybe went back. He was in a long-time college hospital. I think he only spent a couple of days in the hospital. And he was back working as quick as he could.
他试图阻止它，结果和另外两个人一起被冲上了河面。他活了下来，另外两人死了。这个故事似乎引起了人们的关注，因为马歇尔·梅比又回去了。他在一家长效医院呆过。我想他只在医院呆了几天，就尽快回去工作了。

33
00:16:56.000 --> 00:17:15.000
I tell you, you talk to most sandbags and they're going to tell you, one of your times up, your times up. Whether you're walking down the street or working underground, just going to go. You're going to go. When the man says it's time, you're gone. That's all. Simple as that. Just wasn't his time. Stuart Williams thought it was his time a while back.
我告诉你，你跟大多数沙工谈谈，他们都会告诉你，当你的大限已到时，你的大限就到了。不管你是在街上走还是在地下工作，该走的总得走。你总会走的。当上帝说时间到了，你就走了。就是这样，简单明了。只是当时还不是他的时候。斯图尔特·威廉姆斯（Stuart Williams）不久前曾以为自己的大限已到了。

34
00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:40.000
He was working on a subway job when suddenly the tunnel caved in. Stuart, whose only five foot three in ways less than 130 pounds, was nearly crushed to death. Damn, just feeling I ever had. I saw the most beautiful light on my way, my kids just just cleared the day and I passed out. I woke up in the hospital. I broke my leg, my back just threw the head cut open, broke the collarbone shoulder.
他在一个地铁工地工作，突然隧道坍塌了。斯图尔特身高只有五尺三寸，体重不到130磅，差一点被活活压死。该死的，那是我经历过的最奇妙的感觉。我在路上看到了最美丽的微光，我的孩子们刚刚在眼前清晰浮现，然后我就晕厥了。醒来时我已经在医院里了。我断了腿，背部受伤，头部被划破，锁骨和肩膀骨折。

35
00:17:40.000 --> 00:18:25.000
But 8 weeks later, I remember it. 8 weeks. These days Stewart works above ground as a supervisor. Tonight he's directing a 650-pound dynamite blast at chaff 22, part of the water tunnel project in Brooklyn. Chaff 22 is wedged between the Brooklyn Queen's expressway and a row of low-income apartments that look down on the site. It's surrounded by loops of razor wire and bathed in high-intensity floodlights. Stuart blows a whistle once to warn people living in the apartment that an explosion is five minutes away. Dynamite blasts are in almost daily occurrence here. Still, Stuart is anxious. He's pacing back
但8周后，我记得清清楚楚。8周。如今，斯图尔特在地面上担任主管。今晚他在布鲁克林水隧道工程一部分的22号竖井指挥一场650磅的炸药爆破。22号竖井夹在布鲁克林-皇后区高速公路和俯瞰工地的低收入公寓楼之间。周围环绕着刺网圈，沐浴在高强度泛光灯下。斯图尔特吹了一声哨子，警告公寓里的居民五分钟后将发生爆炸。这里几乎每天都会发生炸药爆破。尽管如此，斯图尔特还是很焦虑。他来回踱步，

36
00:18:25.000 --> 00:19:08.000
and forth, smoking a cigarette, nervously pushing the plunger on the empty detonator in and out, and greeting men as they come out of the shaft. How much possible for these men, man. Thank God, that's all I would. I've never hurt one in my life. I've had one get hurt working with me, and I don't want to start now. The one-minute warning, fire officials on hand to monitor the blast, move in closer and put their ear plugs in place. After 35 years of drilling and blasting, Stuart wears hearing aids in both ears. Well, when I started, they didn't have a ear protection they have now.
抽着烟，紧张地按压着空起爆器上的柱塞，并向走出竖井的工人们打招呼。这些人为这些人付出了多少啊，老兄。谢天我，我所能说的就是这些。我这辈子从未伤害过任何人。我从未让任何与我共事的人受伤，我也不想现在就开始。一分钟警告，现场监测爆破的消防官员走近并塞上耳塞。经过35年的钻孔和爆破，斯图尔特双耳都戴着助听器。嗯，我刚开始干的时候，他们可没有现在这种耳部防护。

37
00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:32.000
They tried to tear a rag off for sure for sticking in your ear. The countdown is finally over. Stuart hands the detonator to the blast man who shouts out the final warning. Fire in the hole! Sound is good, sound is good. We'll know when we get down there. That's one of the things about shooting. You never know when you get back down there, what you got.
他们就试着撕下一块破布塞进耳朵里。倒计时终于结束了。斯图尔特将起爆器交给了爆破手，爆破手喊出了最后的警告：炮眼要爆破了！声音不错，声音不错。等我们下去就知道了。这就是爆破的特点之一。你永远不知道当你重新下去时，面对的会是什么。

38
00:19:32.000 --> 00:20:18.000
I got to get the fan. He turns on the fan to clear the smoke out of the tunnel and heads for the Sandhog's locker room, the hog house, located in a nearby trailer for some barbecued ribs and a game of gin rumummy. I love it. I love it. Comerati with the man, the people, I've met some of the greatest people in the world. Worked with some of the greatest people in the world. And you get in and you get into your blood after a while. It's really all you want to do. There is a price Sandhog's pay for this love of the tunnels. You age, you age in the hole, so to speak. Many retired sandhogs, Huey Bar is one of them, suffer from silicosis, from years of breathing
我得把风扇拿来。他打开风扇吹散隧道里的烟雾，然后前往位于附近拖车里的沙工更衣室——“猪屋”（Hog House），去吃点烤排骨，玩一局金拉米纸牌。我爱这一行。我爱它。与这些人、这些人的同事情谊，我遇到过世界上最棒的一些人，与世界上最棒的一些人共事过。一旦你投入其中，它就会融入你的血液。这真的是你唯一想做的事。沙工们对隧道的热爱是有代价的。你会变老，可以说你在井里变老了。许多退休的沙工——休伊·巴尔就是其中之一——由于在隧道里长年呼吸

39
00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:45.000
rock dust down in the tunnels, and caesons disease, a deterioration of the bone from working in compressed air. It puts a heart in on your body, so to speak. You can ask any of the old-timeers that joints hurt, you know, you're raking, you're raking. I don't think there's anyone who works as hard as a hog. Two men would load about a yard of sand in about two and a half to three minutes and this goes on continuously for six hours without a stop. I don't think there's
岩尘而患上了矽肺病，由于在高压环境下工作而患上了减压病（骨质退化）。可以说，这会损害你的身体。你可以问问任何老一辈的人，他们的关节都会痛，你知道的，你得铲土，你得铲土。我认为没有谁的工作能比沙工更辛苦。两个人要在大约两分半到三分钟内装载大约一立方码的沙子，而且这种工作连续进行六个小时一刻不停。我认为没有

40
00:20:45.000 --> 00:21:30.000
only one that stands up with that kind of work. But I never regret it coming in and I'm never ashamed of being what I am. And this is what I am. When the ribbon cutting ceremony is finally held for City Tunnel No. 3, scheduled for completion in the year 2025, most of the sandhogs working on the project will have either retired or have died. 61-year-old Lincoln Richards may not be around, but he says there's satisfaction in just knowing he was part of it. Every time I go down and I come out after eight hours, I say, well, I've made my contribution. And to know what you're doing is that people would be able to enjoy it in the future.
其他人能承受这种工作。但我从未后悔入行，也从不为自己的身份感到羞耻。这就是我。当原定于2025年完工的3号市水隧道最终举行剪彩仪式时，大部分参与该项目的沙工要么已经退休，要么已经离世。61岁的林肯·理查兹可能已经不在了，但他表示，仅仅知道自己曾参与其中就心满意足了。每次我下去，工作八小时后上来，我都说，好吧，我做出了我的贡献。并且知道你在做的事情能让人们在未来享受到它。

41
00:21:30.000 --> 00:22:03.000
Yes, this is something that after I die and go on, it would be still there. Because we're doing something that New York City would always have for the duration. Eddie McGinnis-Fat looks at another way. Eliminate all the tunnels the sand hogs have built over the years the Lincoln the Holland the Brooklyn battery the Long Island and Pennsylvania railroads the subways and you get an idea of the extent to which sand hogs help build New York well a picture a picture of New York City if you will what barges going across bring them people
是的，这就是自我死后多年仍会存在的东西。因为我们正在做的事情会让纽约市永远拥有它。埃迪·麦吉尼斯从另一个角度来看待这个问题。消除沙工多年来建造的所有隧道——林肯隧道、荷兰隧道、布鲁克林电池隧道、长岛和宾夕法尼亚铁路、地铁——你就会明白沙工对建设纽约的贡献有多大。好吧，如果你愿意想象一下纽约市的景象，运送人们过河的驳船，

42
00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:38.000
across and ferries and the best ferry system in the world can carry about 80,000 people in a rush hour. That's like from 6 a.m. to 10 a.m. A tunnel can do that in 20 minutes. Without that progress of people coming back and forth, Manhattan would be a dead island. Manhattan would have been nothing. Why would you build anything for if you couldn't get people in and out? Three years and seven months it took to complete one tube of the Lincoln tunnel.
还有渡轮，世界上最好的渡轮系统在高峰期大约能运载8万人。也就是从早上6点到上午10点。而一条隧道在20分钟内就能做到这一点。如果没有这种人们来往的进步，曼哈顿将是一个死岛，曼哈顿将什么都不是。如果你不能让人流进进出出，你建任何东西又是为了什么？完成林肯隧道的一条管线花费了三年零七个月。

43
00:22:38.000 --> 00:23:22.000
It opened to traffic December 22, 1937. Through the Lincoln tunnel, traffic moves with speed and safety 100 feet below the river. A new link joins the states of New Jersey and New York, a great engineering piece, a great highway, a new conquest of the Hudson. St. Hawks was produced by Dan Collison for Long Hall Productions. Long Hall Productions is Dan Collison and Elizabeth Meister. You can listen to all their stories and they got ton of great ones at longhallpro.org.
它于1937年12月22日对交通开放。通过林肯隧道，交通在河面下100英尺处安全迅捷地运行。一条新纽带连接了新泽西州和纽约州，这是一项伟大的工程，一条伟大的公路，哈德逊河的新征服。《沙工》由丹·科利森为长厅制作公司制作。长厅制作公司由丹·科利森和伊丽莎白·迈斯特（Elizabeth Meister）组成。你可以在longhallpro.org上收听他们的所有故事，那里有大量精彩的内容。

